From 31dfa76ff43de311a8327baa70716c60af10ccfe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruibeikaa <126486262+ruibeikaa@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:30:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] sm_60 MMQ: MoE experts read in place (offset table) and
 the down K loop stopped at K

For Strata's PH402 prompt path.  mul_mat_q gains two template switches, both off by
default (every existing instantiation compiles to the same body):
- pt: a launch's expert zt reads its matrix at x + tab[zt] + add (tab a device array of
  byte offsets from the kernel's const __restrict__ base) instead of x + zt*stride, so
  the experts need not be copied into one strided buffer.  Offsets, not pointers: a
  by-value pointer table went to a stack frame (+12% on down) and a device table of
  pointers lost the restrict provenance (generic LD instead of LDG.E.CI, +7%) on GP100.
- kstop: the K loop runs whole 256-value tiles and peels a last half tile (Q2_0 and
  IQ4_NL half-tile loaders), so a K 640 matrix is not over-read by 128 values - read in
  place those bytes are the next expert's and can decode to inf/NaN.  The dropped half
  met zero q8_1 activations and added +-0: the same bits.
mul_mat_q_case_inplace<type, kstop> (no-fallback configs, tiling kernel only; aborts on
stream-k) and DECL_MMQ_CASE_INPLACE for the caller's instances.
